WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.620
- Okay, I'm rolling.

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:04.460
This video has been a long time coming

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:07.010
and I decided it was finally time for me

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:08.973
to talk about,

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.363
why I left Buzzfeed.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.470
Before I worked at Buzzfeed,

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:20.151
I was just a girl who had
gone viral on Instagram

00:00:20.151 --> 00:00:21.830
with a series of videos,

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.172
called The Girl Who Had
Never Been On A Nice Date.

00:00:24.172 --> 00:00:25.060
A large!

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.500
You got money, he got
money, get it all for him.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.871
And that you know, paid
the bills for a while

00:00:30.871 --> 00:00:33.850
but eventually, that money ran out partly

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:35.990
because I spent it all
on crab leg dinners.

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.870
But also because that's what money does.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.120
And I was like, "Man, I need
to get a job, I need a job.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.090
I need a J-O-B and a
consistent stream of income

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:46.220
so I can stabilize myself."

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:49.440
And then I had a friend, Justin
Kan, who many of you know,

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.140
he was working at Buzzfeed at the time.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.340
He was like, "You should come
and do this taste test video

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.630
where you're gonna taste Doritos."

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.270
I was like, "Okay, yeah all right.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:58.200
I mean, I need some money,
how much y'all paying?"

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.060
And he's like, "$200."

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:00.710
I was like, "To eat Doritos?

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:02.160
I'm coming there!"

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.260
- Interesting and new.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:06.366
- I wish you guys could
taste it, this thing so bad.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:09.610
And I was like, "How does one work here?"

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:11.720
I wound up going to meet

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.807
with the person in charge
at the time he was like,

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:14.810
"You wanna work here?"

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:16.470
And I said, "I don't know
what to tell you people,

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.710
I need a job, I'm broke!"

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:20.090
And so they hired me.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:22.290
I'm so excited it'll just
be the two of us tonight.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:23.920
- Oh no, Zack's coming too.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.680
- Zack and Justin and I,
it formed outta nowhere.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:28.400
It was like, "We have a good thing going.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.300
We got a good give-and-take
and give-and-take."

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.133
- Can I get an amen?

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:31.966
- [Both] Amen.

00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:33.540
- What was special about Zack is,

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.560
him and I had the same sense of humor,

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:36.870
the same reference points.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.430
And then we both started making fun

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.540
of Justin for being bad at technology.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:42.290
- Hey, does anyone have
an iPhone 4 charger?

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:45.550
- I mean, I did back in 2010.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:47.430
- It felt like we were able to make things

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:50.850
based off of what we found
funny very easily together.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.630
This is really weird but, it's okay.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.950
I just don't wanna attend the party.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.200
- Is it something I did?

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.820
- Oh my God Justin, no!

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.070
Are you kidding me, your a dear.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:00.570
I just would rather not

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:02.250
and will not, be attending your party.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.940
This girl Ashly Perez,

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:05.980
who was the complete
opposite of me in every way,

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:08.180
she was optimistic, bubbly and peppy.

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:11.580
She, was insistent on bringing me

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.690
into this world Violet that was happening.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.254
It was a channel on Buzzfeed.

00:02:15.254 --> 00:02:17.630
It was her, Sarah and Ella

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:19.570
and they had these characters.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:20.510
And to me,

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:22.600
it looked like they were making
their own little universe.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:23.810
- If she went anywhere out of character

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:24.810
she would've left a note, right?

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.050
- You're always supposed to
leave a note, she knows that.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.050
We watched 127 Hours together.

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:29.883
- You're right.

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:30.716
- She's fine.

00:02:30.716 --> 00:02:32.077
(cave creature growls)

00:02:32.077 --> 00:02:32.910
I was like, "All right, I'ma get in here

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.040
but I'ma do it my way."

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:35.278
It was fun specially for me

00:02:35.278 --> 00:02:38.980
to kinda be the Black girl representation

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:40.510
in that world they were building.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:41.910
Oh, I'm afraid of the government.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:42.990
No one's policing them,

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:44.800
they can get away with whatever they want.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:46.000
They'll never get me to talk.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.966
- And you're also afraid of love.

00:02:47.966 --> 00:02:48.799
(Quinta squeals)

00:02:48.799 --> 00:02:50.460
- Man okay, the story of Broke.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:52.580
I had this idea of making this show

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:56.930
about three friends in LA who like me,

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:57.990
you know, were broke.

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.870
- We have two pieces of bread.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:02.667
- Hey, an almost empty
jar of peanut butter.

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:04.570
- And a Cup of Noodles.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:05.403
- We could make this work!

00:03:05.403 --> 00:03:08.210
It was a test to see if
they would watch a video

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:11.584
about three Black kids trying to make it.

00:03:11.584 --> 00:03:13.560
(jazz music)

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:14.573
Oh hold up y'all,

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:18.870
we gotta pay rent.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.380
We shot the whole series

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:23.317
and then we were able to sell
the series to YouTube Red.

00:03:23.317 --> 00:03:24.150
- Aye!

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.690
- That was a really cool turning point

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:32.484
for me mentally, as someone
who wanted to make sitcoms.

00:03:32.484 --> 00:03:34.570
- I'm on fire, I'm so on it today.

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:35.770
- I'm sorry, I couldn't hear you

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:38.370
'cause I'm too busy making
strides towards my dream.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:41.360
What are you two doing?

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.230
- Oh man, Oh my God, goin' deep!

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:46.110
Up For Adoption was a show that I made,

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:49.190
that is predecessor to what
I'm making now for ABC.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:52.880
I think style-wise, I was
obsessed like many of us

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.550
with shows like The Office

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:57.410
and Parks and Recreation,
mockumentary style shows.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:02.120
I wanted to try my hand at
making a show about a pet store.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.280
I had gone to one to adopt my cat

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.950
and I was like, "You
people are fascinating.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:07.821
I wanna make a show about you."

00:04:07.821 --> 00:04:09.370
What's wrong?

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.662
(Quinta screams)

00:04:10.662 --> 00:04:11.727
That was the first time I was like,

00:04:11.727 --> 00:04:15.320
"Ooh, I'm making something
that's not based on me."

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:16.796
It made me feel like I had the ability

00:04:16.796 --> 00:04:19.340
to create different worlds

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:22.510
which was really inspiring for me.

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:23.810
Do you want some?

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:25.360
They're for cats and people.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.480
Some of my favorite memories were getting

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:31.210
to be creative in a way that
I don't always get to be now.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:33.463
Let me get you some water
my little sweetheart.

00:04:36.118 --> 00:04:36.951
(Quinta screams)

00:04:36.951 --> 00:04:38.840
Those moments when you
just tell somebody an idea

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.440
and they're like, "Yeah, let's do it!"

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:43.740
We are tasting condoms,
making you proud Mom!

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:45.820
And then also drinking on Fridays,

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:46.870
I miss that a lot.

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:50.320
We used to get really (beep)
drunk on Friday nights.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.420
Drinks for all my friends!

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:53.253
(friends cheer)

00:04:53.253 --> 00:04:55.480
For me, it was time to leave

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:57.910
when my ambitions

00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:00.180
kind of became different

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.880
than just working a nine-to-five.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.450
Requesting time off

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:08.500
to do things like write on a TV show,

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:09.997
and that conflicted

00:05:09.997 --> 00:05:12.750
with keeping a nine-to-five job honestly.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:15.140
For me, it felt like college

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:16.840
and you have to graduate from college.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:19.850
And I think it was really
just time for me to graduate.

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:23.410
In my world, I had no negative experience

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:25.480
that made me wanna leave.

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:28.640
I feel fortunate to
have had the experience.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:32.540
I feel fortunate to have
been able to support myself

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:34.610
and not only my myself, but others.

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:37.820
I was able to support a lot
of other young Black creators

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.340
that, otherwise may
have never had a chance

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.660
in getting in this industry.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:46.310
Quinta Brunson personally,
has nothing but fond memories.

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.600
I looked at it as a really
positive experience for me.

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:51.350
Oh my God, they want the tea.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.060
I think that

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.153
yes,

00:05:55.153 --> 00:05:57.070
but not because I left.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:00.000
YouTube has changed, the
algorithm has changed,

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.610
the Internet has changed.

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:03.390
And I think when I was there,

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:05.306
it was like a special moment in time.

00:06:05.306 --> 00:06:07.430
And not because I was
there but because it was.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.500
YouTube and Facebook and all of that

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:11.000
was in such a, wooo!

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:12.460
Everything was blowing up.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:16.460
It was a crazy phenomenon
of like Wild Wild West,

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:17.900
some Internet creation.

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:20.780
And then I think after a
while, that just died down

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:23.100
as things do sometimes.

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:25.112
That's the cycle of life friends.

00:06:25.112 --> 00:06:27.930
(chuckles) Since I've left Buzzfeed,

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:29.310
I wrote for a TV show

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:30.470
called Lazor Wulf

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:32.310
which was an Adult Swim cartoon.

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:35.010
I was a voice on the popular Netflix show,

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:35.843
Big Mouth,

00:06:35.843 --> 00:06:38.870
and will be returning for
another season of that show.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:42.180
And then I got casted on a show

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:45.490
called Black Lady Sketch
show, which is on HBO.

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:48.360
And that was a really
cool dream come true.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:51.580
I sold a show that I
am super excited about

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:53.750
and super passionate about to ABC

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:55.010
called Abbott Elementary

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:58.170
which will be coming to ABC, very soon.

00:06:58.170 --> 00:06:59.510
You'll actually be able to watch it.

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:01.870
I sold it and it got made and
we're gonna make more of it

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:03.270
and then it's gonna be on TV!

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:06.120
And also, I wrote a book!

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.904
That was a big thing I did.

00:07:07.904 --> 00:07:09.080
This is the part I'm not good at.

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:10.280
If you wanna hear more

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:13.170
about you know my life and stuff,

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:16.650
and even more Buzzfeed juicy tidbits,

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:17.850
you can find it in my book.

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:19.997
I have to do this, I'm obligated to,

00:07:19.997 --> 00:07:21.420
this is what you have to do
when you're promoting a book.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.210
I hate doing this, but I have to do it,

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:25.650
but, it is a good book
and you should read it

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:27.760
if I do say so myself.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:28.840
Not to toot my own horn

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:31.100
but I think I did a
good job with this one.

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:33.075
- [Both] Quinta tripped aye!

00:07:33.075 --> 00:07:35.078
Quinta tripped aye!

00:07:35.078 --> 00:07:35.995
- Whatever.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:40.303
(upbeat music)

